; Route the @harness scope to the Harness Artifact Registry's `ait-commons`
; hosted npm bucket, which is where @harness/ai-test-sdk is published.
; Everything else (Playwright, axios, ...) resolves through the default
; registry.npmjs.org. The bucket is public-read so `npm install` requires
; no auth token.
@harness:registry=https://harness0.harness.io/pkg/l7B_kbSEQD2wjrM7PShm5w/ait-commons/npm/

; --- Private-registry demo (mirrors Wingstop's @wingstop-inc) -----------------
; The @shubham-harness scope is served from GitHub Packages, which requires a
; read:packages token. npm substitutes ${DEMO_REGISTRY_TOKEN} from the process
; environment at install time. If the var is absent/empty, npm sends an empty
; bearer token and GitHub returns 401 — exactly the failure Wingstop hit.
; CHANGE @shubham-harness below if you publish the demo package under a
; different GitHub user/org scope.
@shubham-harness:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${DEMO_REGISTRY_TOKEN}
